      "content": "<h3>Use Vector or something else?</h3>\n<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"8\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse; width:100%;\">\n<tr><th style=\"text-align:left;\">Use Vector when</th><th style=\"text-align:left;\">Use something else when</th></tr>\n<tr><td>You maintain old code that already returns a Vector</td><td>You write new single-threaded code: use <code>ArrayList</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>An old API needs a Vector or an Enumeration</td><td>Many reads and few writes by many threads: use <code>CopyOnWriteArrayList</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>You need a simple thread-safe list and speed is not a worry</td><td>You need atomic multi-step actions: use <code>synchronized</code> blocks or a concurrent collection</td></tr>\n<tr><td>You want to control the growth step with capacityIncrement</td><td>You need a queue between threads: use <code>BlockingQueue</code></td></tr>\n</table>"
